          model: "How to sell a seat at PMT (one page). Know the product: bikes and helmets are provided; the course ends with a certificate the DMV accepts in place of the riding test (confirm exact wording); most students are beginners. Three callers: (1) the nervous first-timer: lead with ‘most people in our classes have never ridden’; (2) the returning rider: lead with getting confident again after years off; (3) the gift buyer: lead with how easy the gift is and the date options. Objections: ‘I've never even sat on a bike’ → that's exactly who the course is built for; ‘It's expensive’ → compare it with buying gear and a bike you might not like, plus the DMV benefit; ‘What if I'm not good enough?’ → explain what happens if someone needs extra practice (confirm PMT's policy). Tone rule: you're inviting someone to something fun, so sound like it, and never read the website at them."
